    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: address normalization on owner creation\n\n**Normalization rules** (trim + collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) live in one new shared utility so store/return and every comparison use identical logic:\n\n- `OwnerAddressNormalizer.java` \u2014 `normalize(String)`; null/whitespace-only \u2192 `\"\"`.\n\n**Wiring into `POST /api/owners`** (`owners.POST.yml`): a new first step `normalizeAddress` runs before `require`:\n\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress.java` \u2014 new entry step. Reads `@RequestBody` once, normalizes the address in place, and republishes the body via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>` for the rest of the pipeline. Because it stores the normalized value on the DTO, `BuildOwner`/the mapper persist and return the normalized `address`.\n\n**Required-field check now sees the normalized address**:\n\n- `RequireOwnerFields.java` \u2014 switched from `@RequestBody`+`Out` to reading the published body via `@Val` (single body-reader, single producer preserved). A blank-after-normalization address is now reported as a missing field \u2192 400.\n\n**Address comparisons use the normalized form**:\n\n- `CheckUniqueOwnerHousehold.java` and `AssignOwnerHousehold.java` \u2014 address comparison (duplicate detection and shared-household-id derivation) now routes both sides through `OwnerAddressNormalizer.normalize`; the last-name helper was renamed to `normalizeName` (unchanged behavior).\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (whitespace/case collapse, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize rejection) \u2014 3/3 pass; full `mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nOne behavioral note worth flagging: since normalization runs before `require`, an address supplied as only whitespace now surfaces as a `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (listed under missing `address`) rather than any downstream validation \u2014 which matches the spec's \"reject an address that is blank after normalization.\"",
